.TH typew 1 "September 2026" "typew 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
typew \- terminal write\-only typewriter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B typew
[\fI\-\-config\fR \fICONFIGFILE\fR | \fI\-c\fR \fICONFIGFILE\fR]
.I FILENAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B typew
is a terminal write\-only typewriter. It loads a
single file, lets you type freely, and write the buffer back to disk on a
timer. It has no load/save commands and keeps the entire file in memory
while you work.
.PP
.I FILENAME
is mandatory and is the file to edit. If it does not exist, it is created.
If it exists, it is read into memory and the cursor is placed on the line
below the last one.
.PP
The active working line is kept in the middle of the terminal. The current
character always blinks. The buffer is saved to disk automatically every
.I save_delay
seconds when there are unsaved changes.
.PP
.B typew
does not save trailing whitespace.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " CONFIGFILE" , \ \fB--config\fR \fICONFIGFILE\fR
Load configuration from
.I CONFIGFILE
instead of the default configuration location (see the
.B CONFIGURATION
section below).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/typew/config
by default (or
.IR ~/.config/typew/config
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset; override with
.BR \-\-config ).
It uses a simple INI\-style
.I key = value
format. Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
are ignored. An example configuration file is written to the default
location the first time the program runs.
.PP
The following keys are supported:
.TP
.BI save_delay
How many seconds to wait before writing the buffer to disk (default
.BR 1.5 ).
.TP
.BI line_endings
The character(s) written at the end of each line (default
.BR \en ).
Options:
.BR \en ,
.BR \er\en ,
.BR \er ,
or any literal string.
.TP
.BI eol_bell
Ring the terminal bell near the end of the writable line (default
.BR true ).
.TP
.BI bell_count
How many characters away from the line end the bell rings (default
.BR 8 ).
.TP
.BI eol_lock
Prevent typing past the end of the line (default
.BR true ).
.TP
.BI line_length
The maximum line length / right margin, and the minimum terminal width
(default
.BR 80 ).
.TP
.BI line_space
How many lines the
.B Return
key advances (default
.BR 1 ).
Arrow keys always move by one line.
.TP
.BI overwrite
The single character used to mark an overwritten position. When you type
over a character that already exists, it is replaced with this character
(default
.BR # ).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Return
Move to the next logical line and return the cursor to the start.
.TP
.B Backspace \fR/\fP Delete
Move the cursor one column left on the current line.
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Move the current character location. You cannot move above line one, but
you can move beyond the last line; you cannot move past the left or right
margin. Typing at a column with empty space inserts leading spaces so the
character lands where you asked.
.TP
.B Escape
Save (if there is anything to save) and quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/typew/config
(or
.IR ~/.config/typew/config )
Default per\-user configuration file, created on first run if missing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate the default configuration file.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
If set, the default configuration file is read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/typew/config
instead of
.IR ~/.config/typew/config .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful termination.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid command line (no
.I FILENAME
given).
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at the typew issue tracker:
https://github.com/josefnpat/typew/issues
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nano (1),
.BR vi (1),
.BR stty (1),
.BR terminfo (5)